      "writtenOn": "2024-05-15T22:59:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wonder if we could avoid the new property by tweaking the variants of the rust modules (assuming mixing the rust and cc dependencies in `static_libs` is even desirable).  Could we assume an incoming dependency with an empty rust_libraries and rust_stdlinkage variations is looking for the rlib?  That becomes much easier to implement after aosp/3077410 lands.",
      "revId": "5540a33e4a8cdc257a4b413e5bb3b033e9273995",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9b793e6c_cca711dc",
        "filename": "cc/cc.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 2645,
      "author": {
        "id": 1115178
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-16T17:01:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could potentially avoid the new property by just checking if a variation exists, e.g.\n\n```\nif OtherModuleDependencyVariantExists(// rust_ffi_variant //) {\n   // link to the rust_ffi_rlib variant\n} else {\n   // attempt to link the rust_ffi_static variant\n}\n```\n\nThe `static_rlibs` property was originally needed for the CreateModule approach. However, I kept it since I think it would still be desirable to clearly indicate in the module definition that we want rlibs bundled into a single generated staticlib.\n\nLonger term, I was thinking we could leave `rust_ffi_static` implemented as a specialized module type for cases where we may need to build some specialized staticlib. In this scenario, once we\u0027ve ported all existing `rust_ffi_static` usage to `rust_ffi_rlib`, Soong would enforce that only one Rust staticlib (either from `static_libs` or `static_rlibs`) shows up in the final link. `rust_ffi` would only produce the rlib and shared variants to further cement that `rust_ffi_static` is a special use-case.\n\nI don\u0027t feel strongly one way or another though -- if you think we should avoid adding the new property then I\u0027m fine implementing something like the above snippet.",
      "parentUuid": "2a62c1e3_c3c66b6c",
      "revId": "5540a33e4a8cdc257a4b413e5bb3b033e9273995",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
